But it provides a fascinating look at what RSVP calls a persistent asymmetry.

29:36.680 --> 29:42.080
When the U.K. left the European Union, the trade costs between the U.K. and the EU obviously

29:42.080 --> 29:48.020
increased due to new customs checks, health certificates for food, and massive bureaucratic friction.

29:48.020 --> 29:54.400
But crucially, the data shows they increased much more than Ireland's trade costs with the EU,

29:54.680 --> 29:56.100
even though Ireland is right next door.

29:56.400 --> 30:00.180
Well, Ireland stayed in the common market, so their logistics remained relatively smooth.

30:00.480 --> 30:05.080
But what is interesting is how the RSVP equations view the U.K.'s situation.

30:05.400 --> 30:11.040
They don't view Brexit as a temporary supply chain blip or a short-term tariff shock.

30:11.260 --> 30:15.240
They view it as a stable, permanent deformation of the cost field.

30:15.240 --> 30:15.720
Yeah.

30:15.940 --> 30:20.220
The regulatory boundary literally warped the invisible geometry of Europe.

30:20.520 --> 30:25.100
Because the direct U.K.-E.U. routes became mathematically inadmissible for certain low-margin

30:25.100 --> 30:29.780
goods due to the new friction, the U.K.'s flow field had to dynamically redirect to seek

30:29.780 --> 30:31.060
out lower constraint regions.

30:31.300 --> 30:32.300
This is trade diversion.

30:32.680 --> 30:34.640
It is a calculated, logistical pivot.

30:34.840 --> 30:35.660
So where did the flow go?

30:35.920 --> 30:40.040
For the U.K., the math found a new path of least resistance, North Africa.

30:40.040 --> 30:44.780
The data shows that the U.K. drastically increased their vegetable imports from Morocco.

30:45.320 --> 30:50.760
Because the Moroccan routes, despite being further away geographically, had a lower invisible

30:50.760 --> 30:56.480
cost in the RSVP manifold than crossing the English Channel with a truck full of tomatoes

30:56.480 --> 30:59.140
that might rot while waiting for customs clearance.

30:59.440 --> 31:03.960
The equations predicted the flow would find the new optimal valley, and the logistics managers

31:03.960 --> 31:07.080
in the U.K. executed exactly what the physics demanded.

31:07.080 --> 31:09.800
OK, let's look at the third example, the phantom wall.

31:10.940 --> 31:12.640
This involves free trade agreements.

31:12.880 --> 31:18.920
Specifically, the data compares the 2015 China-Australia free trade agreement, known as CHAFTA, to

31:18.920 --> 31:24.240
a seemingly routine state visit that Indian Prime Minister Modi made to China in that exact

31:24.240 --> 31:24.900
same year.

31:25.320 --> 31:30.560
And again, remaining politically neutral here, the results completely upend how we view politics.

31:30.980 --> 31:35.740
The data shows that the CHAFTA treaty, this massive, highly publicized, years-in-the-making

31:35.740 --> 31:40.060
political victory, barely affected actual trade costs at all.

31:40.120 --> 31:42.080
It hardly moved the needle in the hidden manifold.

31:42.240 --> 31:42.420
Yeah.

31:42.660 --> 31:44.240
And the math tells us exactly why.

31:44.660 --> 31:49.180
The RSVP accessibility field between Australia and China had already been growing organically

31:49.180 --> 31:50.120
since 2001.

31:50.120 --> 31:57.040
Over 14 years, private businesses built relationships, supply chains were optimized, trust was established,

31:57.460 --> 31:58.800
shipping lanes were streamlined.

31:59.440 --> 32:02.460
The invisible landscape had already smoothed out over a decade.

32:03.040 --> 32:05.380
The 2015 formal treaty didn't lower costs.

32:05.540 --> 32:06.960
The costs were already at rock bottom.

32:07.180 --> 32:11.240
The treaty just put a formal public ribbon on a door that was already wide open.

32:11.240 --> 32:17.180
But conversely, the 2015 Modi visit to China wasn't a massive structural treaty with thousands

32:17.180 --> 32:18.540
of pages of tariff schedules.

32:19.260 --> 32:22.920
Yet, it triggered a sudden massive jump in accessibility for India.

32:23.340 --> 32:25.620
It acted as an informal green light for the market.

32:26.000 --> 32:29.900
The data shows that the invisible cost of the sugar trade from India to China plummeted

32:29.900 --> 32:31.740
by 33% by 2022.

32:32.100 --> 32:37.040
It really highlights a crucial point about the lag between human behavior and bureaucratic reality.

32:37.040 --> 32:42.400
The organic relationship building, the informal trust, the geopolitical signaling, that is

32:42.400 --> 32:44.440
what truly alters the accessibility field.

32:44.960 --> 32:48.120
The formal policy ratification is often just a trailing indicator.

32:48.500 --> 32:51.720
Which brings us to the most radical leap in this entire deep dive.

32:52.260 --> 32:56.760
We have successfully mapped the world's goods, the cargo ships, and the agricultural tariffs

32:56.760 --> 32:58.260
using physics equations.

32:58.560 --> 33:02.720
But the source material asks a terrifyingly ambitious question.

33:02.860 --> 33:03.580
Okay, what is it?

33:03.580 --> 33:09.680
If this math perfectly models the flow of physical cargo, does it also work for the flow of human

33:09.680 --> 33:10.140
lives?

33:10.140 --> 33:14.980
We are expanding the substrate, moving from moving agriculture to moving human beings.

33:15.100 --> 33:20.000
The 2019 Stewart and Wolfram paper proved that this exact mathematical framework works

33:20.000 --> 33:21.600
beautifully for human migration.

33:22.460 --> 33:27.300
Migration flows face their own incredibly complex, often invisible cost landscapes.

33:27.300 --> 33:32.860
Yes, you have visible barriers, visa stringencies, physical border walls, wage differentials

33:32.860 --> 33:33.680
between countries.

33:33.820 --> 33:39.840
But you also have massive unobservables, cultural distance, language barriers, bureaucratic hostility

33:39.840 --> 33:44.400
at a local level, the presence of existing diaspora communities that can help you find a job.

33:44.400 --> 33:45.000
Exactly.

33:45.360 --> 33:48.060
A gravity model cannot quantify a welcoming culture.

33:48.060 --> 33:50.600
But inverse optimal transport can.

33:51.340 --> 33:55.720
By looking at the actual flows of migrants across European borders, the neural networks

33:55.720 --> 33:59.380
can recover the true migration resistance between any two points.

33:59.740 --> 34:05.600
It mathematically calculates the informal, unobservable, cultural barriers that traditional demography

34:05.600 --> 34:06.980
completely misses.

34:07.360 --> 34:12.000
But the Flyxion paper takes this one step further, into what is easily the most speculative,

34:12.300 --> 34:14.180
mind-bending territory we have covered.

34:14.180 --> 34:20.520
It argues that this exact same hidden manifold math, these fluid dynamic equations, apply

34:20.520 --> 34:25.800
not just to moving goods or moving bodies, but to human cognition, to the physical brain

34:25.800 --> 34:26.220
itself.

34:26.460 --> 34:28.320
It is a staggering conceptual leap.

34:28.580 --> 34:32.680
The paper suggests that thoughts and mental states are simply trajectories moving through

34:32.680 --> 34:34.220
a cognitive constraint manifold.

34:34.800 --> 34:37.220
In this model, your conscious attention is the flow field.

34:37.520 --> 34:42.000
Your accumulated knowledge, your trauma, your biases, those represent the structural cost field.

34:42.000 --> 34:46.160
And your cognitive resources, whether you are deeply rested, properly fed, or severely

34:46.160 --> 34:49.600
fatigued, represent the thermodynamic accessibility field.

34:49.920 --> 34:54.560
Are you telling me that my brain experiencing burnout after a long day of work is mathematically

34:54.560 --> 34:57.760
identical to a blocked shipping lane in the Black Sea?

34:58.060 --> 34:59.380
Because how is that possible?

35:00.160 --> 35:01.140
A thought is abstract.

35:01.420 --> 35:03.820
It's an electrical impulse that happens in a millisecond.

35:04.220 --> 35:08.380
How can it be treated like a massive physical cargo ship navigating a tariff?

35:08.380 --> 35:13.860
To understand why the math holds up, we have to look at modern neuroscience, specifically

35:13.860 --> 35:18.520
predictive processing theories, like those developed by the neuroscientist Carl Fristin.

35:19.360 --> 35:22.540
Fristin argues that the human brain is not just a passive computer.

35:22.940 --> 35:27.680
It is literally a prediction engine operating on the principle of free energy minimization.

35:27.920 --> 35:28.060
